(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Watching a Qubit: Continuous Measurement and Quantum Trajectories\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
A computation-first tour of the stochastic master equation, quantum \
trajectories, and the detector record, built from plain matrices in the \
Wolfram Language.\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: August 7, 2026)", "Author",ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Wolfram Research, Inc.", "Affiliation",ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: How This Notebook Flows", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook is a computation-first tour of what happens when you watch a \
quantum system instead of leaving it alone: how the smooth Lindblad master \
equation is really an average over detector records nobody looked at, how \
conditioning on one record turns that smooth equation into a jagged \
stochastic one, how a single step of that stochastic equation can be written \
so the state stays a state, how strong monitoring freezes a qubit while weak \
monitoring lets it drift, how monitored emission sends a pure state wandering \
over the Bloch sphere, and how the detector current, all by itself, carries a \
spectral peak at the qubit's oscillation frequency. Every one of these \
statements is turned into a short piece of code you can run and change.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["\<\
I strongly believe in a computation-first narrative for learning: in a sense, \
if I cannot compute it, I cannot claim to understand it. Real understanding \
shows up when you can do the thing, simulate it, predict it, estimate it, \
rather than repeat words about it. So the rhythm here is always the same: \
state an idea, say it again in plainer words, compute it, then read the \
output aloud and let it raise the next question.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell["\<\
The environment you are reading is a live Wolfram notebook. Evaluate the \
cells from top to bottom; some cells define objects that later cells use, so \
order matters. The story is meant to be read like a movie, one continuous \
take with a few headings for breath, and my suggestion is to look at each \
output and its meaning first, before unpacking every line of the input that \
produced it. You are not locked into the code as given: change a rate, reseed \
the noise, monitor a different operator, and watch what moves. That is the \
whole point of a notebook.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell["\<\
One habit is worth fixing before we start, because it decides what every plot \
in this notebook is allowed to mean. We will constantly produce three \
different kinds of object, and they do not have the same standing:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["Object", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
     Cell["Where it comes from", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
     Cell["What it is", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"]},
   {Cell["A detector current", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"], Cell[
    "the instrument", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"], Cell[
    "observed data", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"]},
   {Cell["A state path computed from a record", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"], Cell[
    "record, model, initial state", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"], Cell[
    "inferred, not directly observed", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "A current and state path from ",
     Cell[BoxData["simulate"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"], 
    Cell["model plus random numbers", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"], Cell[
    "synthetic, useful for insight, not evidence", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "The average of many ",
     Cell[BoxData["simulate"], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
     " runs matched to the master equation"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"], 
    Cell["two calculations of one model", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"], Cell[
    "a check on the code, not a test of nature", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
  GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {
      Scaled[0.14], 
      Scaled[0.37], 
      Scaled[0.37]}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.5}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]], "Text",Express\
ionUUID->"879dba7a-9ddb-4d00-a310-fce9c731814e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, computation plays three roles here: it infers a state from \
data, it illustrates a model by simulation, and it checks code against an \
independent calculation. Keeping those apart is what keeps us honest. We set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " throughout, so every Hamiltonian is measured in inverse time."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell["Prerequisites and How to Read This", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "You should be comfortable with density matrices (a state is a positive, \
unit-trace, Hermitian matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 "), with the matrix exponential, and with the idea of a Wiener increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 ": a zero-mean Gaussian random kick with variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 ", the mathematical version of one tick of white noise. Nothing beyond that \
is assumed. The pace steepens only in Part VIII and the appendix, where we \
ask how small the time step must be; you can read the physics parts first and \
come back to those."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell["Part I: Two Equations, One Monitored Qubit", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Leave a quantum system connected to a large environment (the modes of the \
electromagnetic field, a transmission line, a cavity) but look at none of \
what leaks out. Averaged over everything the environment carries away, the \
state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 " obeys the Lindblad master equation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "\[Rho]"}], "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["c", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["1", "2"], 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["c", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
         StyleBox["c", "TI"]}], ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "}"}], "."}]}]}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, this is the smooth, deterministic equation you get when you \
throw the detector record away. It has no random term, because averaging over \
all possible records has washed the randomness out. Each ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 " is a dissipator: it is how one decay or dephasing channel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 " nudges the state."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A physical state must keep unit trace, so the first thing to check is that \
the dissipator moves probability around without creating or destroying any. \
Build ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 " from plain matrices and confirm it is trace-free for a completely general \
channel and state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"dissipator", "[", 
     RowBox[{"channel_", ",", " ", "state_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"channel", " ", ".", " ", "state", " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "channel", "]"}]}], " ", "-", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "channel", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         "channel", " ", ".", " ", "state"}], " ", "+", "\n", "      ", 
        RowBox[{"state", " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "channel", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         "channel"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
   RowBox[{"dissipator", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"c11", ",", " ", "c12"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"c21", ",", " ", "c22"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"r11", ",", " ", "r12"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"r21", ",", " ", "r22"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the trace of the dissipator vanishes identically, with no \
assumption on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 ". That is exactly why the master equation can be trusted to keep ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 ": dissipation only reshuffles probability."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now put a detector on some of those channels. Monitor operators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " with efficiencies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "\[LessEqual]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "\[LessEqual]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 " (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 " means every photon is caught, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],
 " means none is), and leave the rest, call them ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 ", unwatched. The record you read is random, so the state conditioned on \
that record now obeys a stochastic master equation:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], ",", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SqrtBox[
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", "\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["c", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"c", "\[Rho]"}], "TI"], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["c", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["Tr",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["[",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["c", "TI"], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["c", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox["]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "."}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Equivalently, the smooth master equation has grown one extra term per \
monitored channel, each carrying a Wiener increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 ". That term, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 ", is the measurement backaction: it is how learning something from the \
detector kicks the state. What the detector actually hands you each step is a \
real readout increment"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "=", 
    SqrtBox[
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", 
    StyleBox["Tr",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "+", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In words, the readout is a weak signal (proportional to the expectation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 ") buried in a fresh burst of white noise ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 ". The current an experimenter plots is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The backaction term also has to leave the state normalized: a random kick \
that changed the trace would not preserve probability. That subtraction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 " is precisely what keeps it trace-free. Confirm it for a general channel \
and a unit-trace state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"measurementBackaction", "[", 
     RowBox[{"channel_", ",", " ", "state_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"channel", " ", ".", " ", "state"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"state", " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "channel", "]"}]}], " ", "-", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"channel", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "channel", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", ".",
         " ", "state"}], "]"}], " ", "state"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
    RowBox[{"measurementBackaction", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"c11", ",", " ", "c12"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"c21", ",", " ", "c22"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"r11", ",", " ", "r12"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "r12", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "r11"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
    "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"r11", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As expected, the trace of the backaction also vanishes. So both new pieces, \
the deterministic dissipator and the random backaction, conserve probability, \
and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 " stays a valid state whether or not we keep the record. That is the whole \
logical content of Part I; the rest of the notebook is about computing with \
these two equations. Two limits are worth remembering as checks, and we will \
meet both later: with every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],
 " the record carries no information and the conditional state falls back \
onto the plain master equation, and with every loss channel monitored at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 " a pure state stays pure."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell["Part II: A Step That Stays a State", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The conditional equation is a stochastic differential equation, so the \
obvious way to march it forward is one Euler step: add the drift times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 " and the backaction times the noise. Let us try exactly that and watch it \
break."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "First, the qubit toolkit we will use for the rest of the notebook. The \
lowering operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 " sends ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 ", so in this notebook ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 " is the excited state that decays:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"X", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Y", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Z", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"identity2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"jMinus", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"X", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", "Y"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "stateVector_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "stateVector", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "stateVector", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "state_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
       RowBox[{"state", " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"X", ",", " ", "Y", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"purity", "[", "state_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
     RowBox[{"state", " ", ".", " ", "state"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ket0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ket1", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ketPlus", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "state", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 " returns the three expectation values ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"purity", "[", "state", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 " returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 ", which equals one exactly for a pure state and drops below one for a mixed \
one. When the state is inferred from a record, both of these are inferred \
too; they are not detector readings."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell["\<\
Now the naive Euler step of the conditional equation, for a single monitored \
operator, written straight from the two superoperators above:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"naiveStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"hamiltonian_", ",", " ", "channel_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"state_", ",", " ", "noise_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"state", " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"hamiltonian", " ", ".", " ", "state"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"state", " ", ".", " ", "hamiltonian"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+",
        "\n", "      ", 
       RowBox[{"dissipator", "[", 
        RowBox[{"channel", ",", " ", "state"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "dt"}], 
    " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"measurementBackaction", "[", 
      RowBox[{"channel", ",", " ", "state"}], "]"}], " ", "noise"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Take the equal superposition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 ", monitor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],
 " with no Hamiltonian, and feed in a single noise kick a little larger than \
one standard deviation. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],
 " the signal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],
 " vanishes, so this kick is pure noise. Look at the smallest eigenvalue of \
the result:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"naiveResult", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"naiveStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "identity2"}], ",", " ", "Z", ",", " ", "0.1"}], 
     "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ketPlus", "]"}], ",", " ", "0.5"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Min", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", "naiveResult", "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The smallest eigenvalue is negative. A negative eigenvalue means a negative \
probability, so the Euler step has walked the state clean off the set of \
valid density matrices. The reason is structural: the backaction enters \
linearly in the noise, and a large enough kick overshoots the Bloch ball. \
Shrinking ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 " makes it rarer, but a rare unphysical state is still a broken simulation. \
This forces a better step."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The fix, due to Rouchon and Ralph (",
 ButtonBox["arXiv:1410.5345",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.5345"], None}],
 "), is to write the update as a sum of terms of the form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 " and then renormalize:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["Tr",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{
       UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"],
        LimitsPositioning->False], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]}]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{
       UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
        StyleBox["r", "TI"],
        LimitsPositioning->False], 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         RowBox[{"1", "-", 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]}]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "=", "1", "-", 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.8 Inherited]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"],
      LimitsPositioning->False], 
     RowBox[{
      SqrtBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], " ", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["r", "TI"]], " ", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "."}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The idea is worth saying plainly: if ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 " is positive, then every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 " is positive, a sum of positive matrices is positive, and dividing by a \
positive trace keeps it positive. So a valid state stays valid by \
construction, for any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 " and any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "\[LessEqual]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "\[LessEqual]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 ". (The compact ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 " form of the last term is an exact rewrite of the Milstein double sum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["s", "TI"]]}]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"r", "s"}], "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 "; we test its consequences below rather than take it on faith.)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell["\<\
Build that step from primitives. It reads the fixed model once, then returns \
a function that maps a state and a readout increment to the next state:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rouchonStep", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "hamiltonian_", ",", " ", "monitored_", ",", " ", "efficiencies_", ",", 
     " ", "unmonitored_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"identity", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "hamiltonian", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{"drift", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"I", " ", "hamiltonian"}], " ", "+", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
              "#"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
             RowBox[{"monitored", ",", " ", "unmonitored"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "/",
           "2"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"itoCorrection", " ", "=", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
          RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"#1", " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"#2", " ", ".", " ", "#2"}], ")"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", 
            " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"efficiencies", ",", " ", "monitored"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
          "]"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"state", ",", " ", "readout"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"signal", ",", " ", "m", ",", " ", "updated"}], "}"}], ",", 
         "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"signal", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Total", "@", 
            RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "#2", "]"}], " ", "#1", " ", "#3"}], " ",
                "&"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
               "readout", ",", " ", "efficiencies", ",", " ", "monitored"}], 
               "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"identity", " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"drift", " ", "dt"}], " ", "+", " ", "signal", " ", "+", 
            " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"signal", " ", ".", " ", "signal"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-",
             " ", 
            RowBox[{"itoCorrection", " ", "dt"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"updated", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"m", " ", ".", " ", "state", " ", ".", " ", 
             RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "m", "]"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", 
            "      ", 
            RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"#", " ", ".", " ", "state", " ", ".", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], 
               " ", "/@", " ", "unmonitored"}], "]"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", 
            "      ", 
            RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
              RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                   RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ")"}], " ", 
                  RowBox[{"#1", " ", ".", " ", "state", " ", ".", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#1", "]"}]}]}], " ", 
                 "&"}], ",", "\n", "         ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"monitored", ",", " ", "efficiencies"}], "}"}]}], 
               "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"updated", "/", 
           RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "updated", "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now revisit the exact kick that broke the Euler step, the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],
 ", the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],
 ", the same noise (which at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 " is the whole readout increment), and read the smallest eigenvalue again:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rouchonResult", " ", "=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"rouchonStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "identity2"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "Z", "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "0.1"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ketPlus", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "0.5", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Min", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", "rouchonResult", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "rouchonResult", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],

Cell["\<\
The smallest eigenvalue is now zero to roundoff and the trace is one: the \
step that overshot the ball now lands on its surface. Positivity is no longer \
a matter of luck with the step size.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With one physical step in hand, two small functions finish the toolkit. The \
first generates a synthetic record: at each step it draws a Wiener increment, \
turns it into a readout ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "R"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 " through the signal-plus-noise rule, and advances the state. It returns the \
state path, the record, and the noise it drew:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"readoutIncrement", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "state_", ",", " ", "monitored_", ",", " ", "efficiencies_", ",", " ", 
      "dt_", ",", " ", "noise_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "#3", "]"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
          RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"#1", " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#1", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", ".",
             " ", "state"}], "]"}]}], " ", "dt"}], " ", "+", " ", "#2"}], " ",
        "&"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"monitored", ",", " ", "noise", ",", " ", "efficiencies"}], 
       "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "initialState_", ",", " ", "hamiltonian_", ",", " ", "monitored_", ",", 
      " ", "efficiencies_", ",", " ", "unmonitored_", ",", "\n", "   ", "dt_",
       ",", " ", "finalTime_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"stepCount", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
          RowBox[{"finalTime", "/", "dt"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "step", ",", 
        " ", "noise", ",", " ", "states", ",", " ", "record"}], "}"}], ",", 
      "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"step", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"rouchonStep", "[", 
         RowBox[{
         "hamiltonian", ",", " ", "monitored", ",", " ", "efficiencies", ",", 
          " ", "unmonitored", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"noise", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dt", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"stepCount", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", "monitored", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";",
        "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"states", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"state", ",", " ", "dW"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
            RowBox[{"step", "[", 
             RowBox[{"state", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"readoutIncrement", "[", 
               RowBox[{
               "state", ",", " ", "monitored", ",", " ", "efficiencies", ",", 
                " ", "dt", ",", " ", "dW"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
          "\n", "    ", "initialState", ",", " ", "noise"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
       "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"record", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"readoutIncrement", "[", 
            RowBox[{
            "#1", ",", " ", "monitored", ",", " ", "efficiencies", ",", " ", 
             "dt", ",", " ", "#2"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Most", "[", "states", "]"}], ",", " ", "noise"}], 
           "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<Times\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "stepCount"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<States\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "states"}], ",", "\n", 
         "   ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Record\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "record"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Noise\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "noise"}]}], "|>"}]}]}], 
     "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "initialState_", ",", " ", "hamiltonian_", ",", " ", "monitored_", ",", 
     " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "finalTime_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "initialState", ",", " ", "hamiltonian", ",", " ", "monitored", ",", "\n",
      "   ", 
     RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
      RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Length", "[", "monitored", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "finalTime"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],

Cell["\<\
The second uses a record you supply and never draws a random number. This is \
the function to point at calibrated experimental data:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"infer", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "initialState_", ",", " ", "hamiltonian_", ",", " ", "monitored_", ",", 
      " ", "efficiencies_", ",", " ", "unmonitored_", ",", "\n", "   ", "dt_",
       ",", " ", "record_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"<|", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<Times\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dt", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Length", "[", "record", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
      "   ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<States\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"rouchonStep", "[", 
          RowBox[{
          "hamiltonian", ",", " ", "monitored", ",", " ", "efficiencies", ",",
            " ", "unmonitored", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         "initialState", ",", " ", "record"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Record\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "record"}]}], "|>"}]}], ";"}],
   "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"infer", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "initialState_", ",", " ", "hamiltonian_", ",", " ", "monitored_", ",", 
     " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "record_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"infer", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "initialState", ",", " ", "hamiltonian", ",", " ", "monitored", ",", "\n",
      "   ", 
     RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
      RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Length", "[", "monitored", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "record"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The short call form of each function assumes unit efficiency and no \
unwatched channel; we turn those knobs in Part VII. Notice the deliberate \
split: ",
 Cell[BoxData["simulate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],
 " contains the only random-number generator in the notebook and its outputs \
are synthetic, while ",
 Cell[BoxData["infer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],
 " is deterministic given its record. That split is the honest boundary \
between a model and a measurement, and Part III makes it concrete. For a \
hardened, dimension-general version of exactly this integrator with full \
input checking, see the companion package ",
 Cell["manual-implementation-ito-qf-independent.wl", "InlineCode",
  ExpressionUUID->"78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 " in this folder; here we keep the step bare so the machinery stays \
visible."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell["\<\
Part III: One Trajectory, and the Average Is the Master Equation\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the heart of the notebook, so we build it around one model and look \
at it from every side. Drive a qubit with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "=", "\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 ", start it in the excited state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],
 ", and monitor its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],
 " component through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"omega", " ", "=", " ", "1.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gamma", " ", "=", " ", "0.4"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hamiltonian", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"omega", " ", "X"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"measuredOperators", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "gamma", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"initialState", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ket0", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"finalTime", " ", "=", " ", "10.0"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To have an independent standard to compare against, solve the smooth master \
equation directly with a differential-equation solver. This is a completely \
separate calculation from the trajectory stepper: no Rouchon step, no random \
numbers, just ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolveValue"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],
 " on the Lindblad equation:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"masterEquationSolution", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "initialState_", ",", " ", "hamiltonian_", ",", " ", "channels_", ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"t_", ",", " ", "t0_", ",", " ", "t1_"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
    ":=", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"state", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"hamiltonian", " ", ".", " ", 
              RowBox[{"state", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"state", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
              "hamiltonian"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"dissipator", "[", 
              RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"state", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
             " ", "channels"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"state", "[", "t0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         "initialState"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "state", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "t0", ",", " ", "t1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}],
   "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"masterSolution", " ", "=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"masterEquationSolution", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "initialState", ",", " ", "hamiltonian", ",", " ", "measuredOperators", ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "finalTime"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[11]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Generate one record and its state path, and plot the monitored component ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 " against the smooth master-equation curve:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"oneRun", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "1", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "initialState", ",", " ", "hamiltonian", ",", " ", "measuredOperators", 
       ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "finalTime"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"timeGrid", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"oneRun", "[", "\"\<Times\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"masterStates", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"masterSolution", " ", "/@", " ", "timeGrid"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"timeGrid", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "#", "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"oneRun", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"timeGrid", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "#", "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         "masterStates"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.6", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", "Red"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<one record\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<master equation\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[LeftAngleBracket]Z\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<One jagged record against the smooth average\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[12]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, the single record jitters constantly and never sits on the \
smooth curve. That is the correct picture, not a numerical defect: the smooth \
curve is the average over all possible records, and no individual record \
follows an average, just as no single coin flip equals one half.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before trusting that jagged path, confirm it is genuinely inferable and not \
an artifact of the random draw. Feed the record ",
 Cell[BoxData["simulate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 " produced back into ",
 Cell[BoxData["infer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 " and compare the two state paths:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"inferred", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"infer", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "initialState", ",", " ", "hamiltonian", ",", " ", "measuredOperators", ",",
      " ", "dt", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"oneRun", "[", "\"\<Record\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ",", " ", "\"\<Frobenius\>\""}], 
     "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "@@@", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"oneRun", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"inferred", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[13]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two paths coincide exactly, because they fold the same update rule over \
the same record. This is the sim-to-experiment bridge in miniature: with real \
data you would drop the record ",
 Cell[BoxData["simulate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],
 " invented and hand ",
 Cell[BoxData["infer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 " the calibrated detector increments instead, and the state path would come \
out the same way."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],

Cell["\<\
Now the central claim. If the smooth curve really is the average over \
records, then averaging many independent trajectories should reproduce it. \
Average one hundred and fifty runs and measure the largest gap to the master \
equation over the whole time interval:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"manyStates", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "42", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
         RowBox[{
         "initialState", ",", " ", "hamiltonian", ",", " ", 
          "measuredOperators", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "finalTime"}], "]"}],
         "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "150", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"meanStates", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "manyStates", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ",", " ", "\"\<Frobenius\>\""}], 
     "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "@@@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"meanStates", ",", " ", "masterStates"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[14]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The gap is small, and it is Monte Carlo scatter: it shrinks like one over \
the square root of the number of runs, not because the two calculations are \
secretly the same code, but because the random backaction has exactly the \
right mean. Plot the averaged ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],
 " on top of the master-equation curve to see them lie together:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"timeGrid", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "#", "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         "meanStates"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"timeGrid", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "#", "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         "masterStates"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", "Red"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<mean of 150 records\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<master equation\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[LeftAngleBracket]Z\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Averaging the records rebuilds the smooth equation\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[15]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell["\<\
Averaging over records is the whole meaning of the word unravelling: the \
deterministic master equation is what you get by forgetting which record \
occurred.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],

Cell["\<\
That forgetting has a sharp signature in the purity. With the channel \
monitored at unit efficiency, every single record keeps the state pure, while \
the average over records is mixed. Compare the purity of one record with the \
purity of the averaged state, along the whole path:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"timeGrid", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"oneRun", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"timeGrid", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", "meanStates"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", "Red"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<one record\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<average over records\>\""}],
      "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<purity  Tr[\[Rho]^2]\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0.45", ",", " ", "1.03"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<A kept record stays pure; the average decoheres\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[16]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],

Cell["\<\
Here is the payoff of the whole part: decoherence is not something that \
happens to a monitored qubit. Each record leaves it perfectly pure. \
Decoherence is what you see when you average over the records you chose not \
to keep. Ordinary open-system decay is monitored dynamics with the detector \
switched off.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],

Cell["\<\
Before moving on, let us summarize the most important points we have computed \
so far:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The dissipator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],
 " and the backaction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],
 " are both trace-free, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],
 " stays a unit-trace state with or without the record."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A naive Euler step of the conditional equation can produce a negative \
eigenvalue; the Rouchon step writes the update as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Sum]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],
 " and stays positive by construction."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One record gives a jagged ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],
 " that never sits on the smooth master-equation curve."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Feeding a simulated record into ",
 Cell[BoxData["infer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 " reproduces the simulated state path exactly."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],

Cell["\<\
The average of many records reproduces the master equation, with only Monte \
Carlo scatter left over.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],

Cell["\<\
Each unit-efficiency record stays pure; the average is mixed. Decoherence is \
the average over discarded records.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],

Cell["Part IV: Strong and Weak Monitoring", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What does monitoring strength do to the qubit? For our model, the \
record-averaged ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],
 " obeys a damped-oscillator equation that we can read off and check by \
hand:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], ".."], "+", "2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "."], "+", "4", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "=", "0"}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", "1"}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["z", "TI"], "."], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", "0"}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"exponents", "\[NonBreakingSpace]"}],
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]", 
     RowBox[{
      SqrtBox[
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "-", "4", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"]}]], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, the drive ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],
 " wants to rotate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 " (the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 " restoring term) and the monitoring ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],
 " wants to damp it. Before choosing any numbers, verify the equation, both \
initial conditions, and the strong-monitoring rate symbolically:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"symbolicZ", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "symbolicGamma"}], " ", "symbolicTime"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Cosh", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"symbolicGamma", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"4", " ", 
            RowBox[{"symbolicOmega", "^", "2"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
         "symbolicTime"}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"symbolicGamma", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sinh", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"symbolicGamma", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{"4", " ", 
              RowBox[{"symbolicOmega", "^", "2"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
           "symbolicTime"}], "]"}], "/", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"symbolicGamma", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"4", " ", 
            RowBox[{"symbolicOmega", "^", "2"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
   ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"D", "[", 
       RowBox[{"symbolicZ", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"symbolicTime", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", 
      "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "symbolicGamma", " ", 
       RowBox[{"D", "[", 
        RowBox[{"symbolicZ", ",", " ", "symbolicTime"}], "]"}]}], " ", "+", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", 
       RowBox[{"symbolicOmega", "^", "2"}], " ", "symbolicZ"}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"symbolicZ", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"symbolicTime", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"D", "[", 
       RowBox[{"symbolicZ", ",", " ", "symbolicTime"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"symbolicTime", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"symbolicGamma", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"symbolicGamma", " ", "-", "\n", "       ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"symbolicGamma", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"4", " ", 
             RowBox[{"symbolicOmega", "^", "2"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"symbolicGamma", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"symbolicGamma", " ", ">", " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "symbolicOmega"}], " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[17]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The four entries come back as the equation residual, the value at zero, the \
derivative at zero, and the strong-monitoring slow-rate coefficient. The \
first three confirm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],
 " solves the problem; the last says that when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[GreaterGreater]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],
 " the slow exponent is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "-", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"], "-", "4", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"]}]], "\[TildeEqual]", "2", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 ". Read that rate plainly: stronger monitoring makes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],
 " change more slowly. Watching the qubit freezes it, an instance of the \
quantum Zeno effect."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell["\<\
Package the exact solution so we can plot it in either regime:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"zDephasing", "[", 
    RowBox[{"t_", ",", " ", "omega_", ",", " ", "gamma_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"q", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"gamma", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", 
         RowBox[{"omega", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Which", "[", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"q", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "gamma"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Cosh", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "q", "]"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gamma", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sinh", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "q", "]"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], "/", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "q", "]"}]}]}]}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       
       RowBox[{"q", " ", "<", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "gamma"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
             RowBox[{"-", "q"}], "]"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gamma", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
               RowBox[{"-", "q"}], "]"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], "/", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
             RowBox[{"-", "q"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       "True", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "gamma"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"gamma", " ", "t"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[18]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell["\<\
Choose one strong rate and one weak rate, well separated, and plot the two \
exact curves:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"omegaD", " ", "=", " ", "1.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gammaStrong", " ", "=", " ", "20.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gammaWeak", " ", "=", " ", "0.1"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"timeGridD", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "8.0", ",", " ", "0.0025"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"timeGridD", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"zDephasing", "[", 
         RowBox[{"timeGridD", ",", " ", "omegaD", ",", " ", "gammaStrong"}], 
         "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"timeGridD", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"zDephasing", "[", 
         RowBox[{"timeGridD", ",", " ", "omegaD", ",", " ", "gammaWeak"}], 
         "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<strong monitoring: barely moves\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<weak monitoring: oscillates\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[LeftAngleBracket]Z\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Strong monitoring freezes Z; weak monitoring lets it \
swing\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[19]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As expected, the strongly monitored qubit clings to its initial ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],
 " while the weakly monitored one swings freely under the drive. Confirm that \
the independent master-equation solver agrees with the exact curve in both \
regimes:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"strongMaster", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"masterEquationSolution", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ket0", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"omegaD", " ", "X"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "gammaStrong", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8.0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"weakMaster", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"masterEquationSolution", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ket0", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"omegaD", " ", "X"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "gammaWeak", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8.0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}],
   "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
           RowBox[{"strongMaster", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
        "timeGridD"}], ")"}], " ", "-", "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{"zDephasing", "[", 
       RowBox[{"timeGridD", ",", " ", "omegaD", ",", " ", "gammaStrong"}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
           RowBox[{"weakMaster", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
        "timeGridD"}], ")"}], " ", "-", "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{"zDephasing", "[", 
       RowBox[{"timeGridD", ",", " ", "omegaD", ",", " ", "gammaWeak"}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[20]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both gaps are at solver tolerance. Now the individual records, which the \
smooth curves hide. Run one trajectory in each regime and plot the inferred \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"strongRun", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "7", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ket0", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"omegaD", " ", "X"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "gammaStrong", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", 
       " ", "0.0025", ",", " ", "8.0"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"weakRun", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "7", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ket0", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"omegaD", " ", "X"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "gammaWeak", "]"}], " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", 
        " ", "0.0025", ",", " ", "8.0"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"strongRun", "[", "\"\<Times\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "#", "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"strongRun", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], 
     ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"weakRun", "[", "\"\<Times\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "#", "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"weakRun", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<strong: one record\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<weak: one record\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<inferred \[LeftAngleBracket]Z\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1.05"}], ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Individual records: pinned near an eigenstate versus free to \
drift\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[21]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The strongly monitored record stays pinned near a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 " eigenstate for long stretches, with occasional abrupt hops: the continuous \
limit of quantum jumps. The weakly monitored record wanders with the drive. \
These paths illustrate the model; only a detector record from a real device \
could support a claim about a real device."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],

Cell["Part V: Monitored Spontaneous Emission", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So far we monitored a Hermitian operator, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],
 ". Monitoring emission is different, because the jump operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],
 " is not Hermitian. In homodyne detection the instrument beats the emitted \
light against a reference and records one real quadrature of the field. With \
a complete, unit-efficiency record and a pure initial state, the inferred \
state stays pure, so it lives on the surface of the Bloch sphere and we can \
watch it move there."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Set up a driven, detuned qubit whose emission ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["S", "TI"]]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 " is monitored by homodyne detection, starting from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"omegaS", " ", "=", " ", "2.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"detuningS", " ", "=", " ", "1.0"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hamiltonianS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"omegaS", " ", "X"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"detuningS", " ", "Z"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gammaS", " ", "=", " ", "0.2"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"measuredS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "gammaS", "]"}], " ", "jMinus"}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"initialStateS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ketPlus", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dtS", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"finalTimeS", " ", "=", " ", "10.0"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[22]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],

Cell["\<\
Generate five independent records and turn each state path into a curve of \
Bloch vectors:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"emissionRuns", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "3", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "initialStateS", ",", " ", "hamiltonianS", ",", " ", "measuredS", ",",
          " ", "dtS", ",", " ", "finalTimeS"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "5", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"emissionBlochPaths", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
     " ", "emissionRuns"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[23]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],

Cell["\<\
Draw a bare Bloch sphere and overlay the five inferred paths:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochSphere", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Graphics3D", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.12", "]"}], ",", " ", "LightBlue", ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sphere", "[", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "1.1"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",",
              " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"1.1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], 
           "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"-", "1.1"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], 
           "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"-", "1.1"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1.1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], 
           "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Boxed", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "1.15"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "420"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Show", "[", 
  RowBox[{"blochSphere", ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Graphics3D", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Thick", ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"MapIndexed", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
            RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"First", "@", "#2"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Line", "@", "#1"}]}], "}"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
        "emissionBlochPaths"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[24]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],

Cell["\<\
Each curve is one possible inferred state path for one possible record, \
wandering on the surface as the detector delivers its noisy quadrature. Now \
watch what averaging does: run many records and compare the mean state with \
the master equation:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"emissionMaster", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"masterEquationSolution", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "initialStateS", ",", " ", "hamiltonianS", ",", " ", "measuredS", ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "finalTimeS"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"emissionTimeGrid", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"emissionRuns", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Times\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"emissionMeanStates", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Mean", "@", 
     RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "11", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
           RowBox[{
           "initialStateS", ",", " ", "hamiltonianS", ",", " ", "measuredS", ",",
             " ", "dtS", ",", " ", "finalTimeS"}], "]"}], 
          "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "150", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ",", " ", "\"\<Frobenius\>\""}], 
     "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "@@@", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"emissionMeanStates", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"emissionMaster", " ", "/@", " ", "emissionTimeGrid"}]}], "}"}],
     "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[25]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell["\<\
The mean tracks the master equation to Monte Carlo scatter. So the \
surface-wandering pure records, averaged together, sink into the ball and \
decay toward the ground state: ordinary spontaneous decay is the averaged, \
unwatched version of these jittering pure trajectories, exactly the lesson of \
Part III now carried over from a Hermitian channel to an emission channel.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell["Part VI: What the Detector Record Shows", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],

Cell["\<\
The state paths we have plotted are inferred objects. The detector current is \
not: it is the raw thing the instrument produces, and its statistics are \
observable without any model. From one long current we can compute its mean, \
how readings separated in time move together, and how its power is spread \
over frequency. The last two are the autocovariance and the power spectrum.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],

Cell["\<\
Take a driven, emitting qubit and record for a long time so the statistics \
settle:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"omegaC", " ", "=", " ", "3.5"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gammaC", " ", "=", " ", "0.7"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hamiltonianC", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"omegaC", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Y", "/", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"measuredC", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "gammaC", "]"}], " ", "jMinus"}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"dtC", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
   RowBox[{"finalTimeC", " ", "=", " ", "1200.0"}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"longRun", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "1", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ket0", "]"}], ",", " ", "hamiltonianC", 
       ",", " ", "measuredC", ",", " ", "dtC", ",", " ", "finalTimeC"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"simulatedCurrent", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"longRun", "[", "\"\<Record\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", "dtC"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[26]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A single current sample is almost all noise. Confirm that its standard \
deviation is set by the white-noise level ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],
 ", not by the signal:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "simulatedCurrent", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "simulatedCurrent", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dtC", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[27]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The mean is small and the spread matches ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 ": one reading tells you next to nothing. The coherent motion is hiding in \
the correlations between readings. The autocovariance measures how readings \
separated by a delay move together; compute it with a fast Fourier transform, \
dividing each delay by its own number of data pairs:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"autocovariance", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "data_", ",", " ", "maximumLag_Integer", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"stride_Integer", " ", ":", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"centered", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"N", "[", 
          RowBox[{"data", " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "data", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"count", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "data", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "paddedLength", ",",
         " ", "sums", ",", " ", "lags"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"lags", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
           RowBox[{"maximumLag", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"count", " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          "stride"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"paddedLength", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", "^", 
         RowBox[{"Ceiling", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Log", "[", 
           RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "count"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], 
          "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"sums", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
         RowBox[{"InverseFourier", "[", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
                RowBox[{"centered", ",", " ", "paddedLength"}], "]"}], ",", 
               "\n", "        ", 
               RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], ",",
            " ", 
           RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"dt", " ", "lags"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"sums", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"lags", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"count", " ", "-", " ", "lags"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], 
        "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"currentCovariance", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Rest", "@", 
     RowBox[{"autocovariance", "[", 
      RowBox[{"simulatedCurrent", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
        RowBox[{"8", "/", "dtC"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "dtC", ",", " ", "4"}], 
      "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"currentCovariance", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<lag\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<current autocovariance\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<A driven oscillation survives inside the noisy current\>\""}]}],
   "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[28]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],

Cell["\<\
We drop the zero-lag point because it holds the large white-noise variance; \
away from it, the autocovariance oscillates at the driven frequency. So the \
coherent motion that no single reading revealed is plainly there once we \
correlate readings across time. The same information, sorted by frequency \
instead of by delay, is the power spectrum. Estimate it by splitting the \
record into segments, removing each segment's mean, and averaging the segment \
spectra:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"averagedPeriodogram", "[", 
     RowBox[{"data_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "segmentLength_Integer"}], 
     "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"segments", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Partition", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"N", "[", "data", "]"}], ",", " ", "segmentLength", ",", 
           " ", "segmentLength"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "twoSided", ",", "\n", 
        "   ", "meanSpectrum", ",", " ", "indices", ",", " ", "frequencies"}],
        "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"twoSided", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"dt", "/", "segmentLength"}], ")"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\n", "       ", 
             RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"#", " ", "-", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "#", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}],
           " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "segments"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"meanSpectrum", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "twoSided", "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"indices", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Ceiling", "[", 
           RowBox[{"segmentLength", "/", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
       "  ", 
       RowBox[{"frequencies", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Length", "[", "indices", "]"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"segmentLength", " ", "dt"}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"frequencies", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", 
           RowBox[{"meanSpectrum", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "indices", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}]}], 
     "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"spectrum", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"averagedPeriodogram", "[", 
      RowBox[{"simulatedCurrent", ",", " ", "dtC", ",", " ", "4096"}], "]"}], 
     ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"First", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "<=", " ", "8"}], " ", "&"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"oscillationFrequency", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"omegaC", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"gammaC", "^", "2"}], "/", "16"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"spectrum", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "oscillationFrequency", "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<angular frequency\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<one-sided power spectrum\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<A peak rises above the flat white-noise floor\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[29]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Under this one-sided convention ideal white noise sits at a flat level of \
two, and above it a peak rises in the driven band. Where should it sit? The \
record-averaged coherence oscillates at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["osc",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", 
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"], "-", 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"], "/", "16"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],
 " and decays at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],
 ", so the line is centered at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["osc",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],
 " with a half width of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],
 ". A single noisy periodogram cannot pin a broad line to one bin, so instead \
of reading the argmax, compare the mean power in that predicted band with a \
control band away from it, against the white-noise floor of two:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"halfWidth", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"3", " ", 
    RowBox[{"gammaC", "/", "4"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"bandPower", "[", 
     RowBox[{"spectrum_", ",", " ", "center_", ",", " ", "width_"}], "]"}], 
    " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Mean", "@", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
       RowBox[{"spectrum", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"center", " ", "-", " ", "width"}], " ", "<=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"First", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "<=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"center", " ", "+", " ", "width"}]}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], 
  "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"bandPower", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "spectrum", ",", " ", "oscillationFrequency", ",", " ", "halfWidth"}], 
    "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"bandPower", "[", 
    RowBox[{"spectrum", ",", " ", "1.0", ",", " ", "halfWidth"}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[30]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],

Cell["\<\
The predicted band carries power well above two while the control band sits \
at the floor: the coherent line lives exactly where the model puts it. That \
is the honest reach of this section. The mean, the autocovariance, and the \
excess power are genuine observed features of the current, computed from the \
record alone, while turning that line into a precise frequency or a decay \
rate needs a longer record or a model fit, not a width read off by eye.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],

Cell["Part VII: Efficiency and Dimension", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two knobs on the toolkit have been sitting at their defaults. Detection \
efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],
 " changes the record-based state estimate, though not the master equation \
you get after averaging. Turn it below one and the conditional state can no \
longer stay pure: you are catching only a fraction of the emitted \
information, and the fraction you miss mixes your estimate. Compare one \
record at full efficiency with one at half efficiency, driven along the same \
noise seed:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"omegaE", " ", "=", " ", "2.0"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gammaE", " ", "=", " ", "1.0"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hamiltonianE", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"omegaE", " ", 
    RowBox[{"X", "/", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"measuredE", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "gammaE", "]"}], " ", "jMinus"}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"initialStateE", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ketPlus", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"dtE", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
   RowBox[{"finalTimeE", " ", "=", " ", "6.0"}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fullEfficiency", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "5", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "initialStateE", ",", " ", "hamiltonianE", ",", " ", "measuredE", ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "1.0", "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "dtE", ",", " ", "finalTimeE"}], "]"}]}],
     "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"halfEfficiency", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "5", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "initialStateE", ",", " ", "hamiltonianE", ",", " ", "measuredE", ",", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "0.5", "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "dtE", ",", " ", "finalTimeE"}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"purity", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}], " ", 
      "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"fullEfficiency", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{"purity", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"halfEfficiency", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[31]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],

Cell["\<\
The full-efficiency record stays pure to roundoff; the half-efficiency record \
is mixed, its mean purity well below one. In short, efficiency is how much of \
the environment's information you actually hold, and holding less of it \
leaves you with a more uncertain, more mixed estimate.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now confirm that averaging over records erases ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],
 " entirely. Take three efficiencies, and for each average the final state \
over many records and compare with the single master-equation solution:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"efficiencyMaster", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"masterEquationSolution", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "initialStateE", ",", " ", "hamiltonianE", ",", " ", "measuredE", ",", 
      "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "finalTimeE"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}],
    ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1.0", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "0.0"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"efficiency", ",", " ", "seed"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Mean", "@", 
           RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "        ", 
             
             RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                  "initialStateE", ",", " ", "hamiltonianE", ",", " ", 
                   "measuredE", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"{", "efficiency", "}"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", "\n", "           ", "dtE", ",", 
                   " ", "finalTimeE"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", 
                 RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", "100", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", "\n", 
          "      ", 
          RowBox[{"efficiencyMaster", "[", "finalTimeE", "]"}]}], ",", 
         " ", "\"\<Frobenius\>\""}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1.0", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "0.0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"101", ",", " ", "102", ",", " ", "103"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[32]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All three efficiencies land on the same master-equation state within Monte \
Carlo scatter. So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],
 " reshapes every individual record but leaves their average untouched: the \
unwatched master equation cannot tell how efficiently you were watching."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The second knob is dimension. Nothing in ",
 Cell[BoxData["rouchonStep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],
 " assumed a qubit; it read the dimension from the Hamiltonian. Monitor a \
spin-one system through its lowering operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],
 " and drive it with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["J", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["J", "TI"], "-"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["J", "TI"], "+"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"jMinus3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}],
      ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"jX3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"jMinus3", " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "jMinus3", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
    "2"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hamiltonian3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"1.5", " ", "jX3"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"measured3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "0.6", "]"}], " ", "jMinus3"}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"initialState3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dt3", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"finalTime3", " ", "=", " ", "8.0"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[33]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run one qutrit record at efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "0.4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],
 " and check it stays a physical state by reading its smallest eigenvalue \
along the path:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qutritRun", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "2", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "initialState3", ",", " ", "hamiltonian3", ",", " ", "measured3", ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "0.4", "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "dt3", ",", " ", "finalTime3"}], "]"}]}],
     "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"#", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], 
      "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"qutritRun", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[34]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],

Cell["\<\
The smallest eigenvalue never goes negative: the positivity argument never \
mentioned the dimension, so it holds here unchanged. Finally, average the \
full qutrit density matrix over many records and compare with its master \
equation:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qutritMaster", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"masterEquationSolution", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "initialState3", ",", " ", "hamiltonian3", ",", " ", "measured3", ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "finalTime3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"qutritMean", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Mean", "@", 
     RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "9", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
           RowBox[{
           "initialState3", ",", " ", "hamiltonian3", ",", " ", "measured3", ",",
             " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "0.4", "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "dt3", ",", "\n", "       ", 
            "finalTime3"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "120", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ",", " ", "\"\<Frobenius\>\""}], 
     "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "@@@", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"qutritMean", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"qutritMaster", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"qutritRun", "[", "\"\<Times\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[35]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],

Cell["\<\
The full three-by-three mean matches the master equation, populations and \
coherences alike. Monitoring, unravelling, and the master-equation-as-average \
picture were never facts about qubits; they are facts about open quantum \
systems of any size.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],

Cell["Part VIII: Can We Trust This Step Size?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every plot above used a fixed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],
 ", and the Rouchon step earns its keep by guaranteeing a valid state at any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],
 ". But a valid state is not the same as an accurate one. In other words, \
positivity is a physicality check, not an error estimate: a positive density \
matrix can still be the wrong positive density matrix if the step is too \
coarse. So the step size needs a separate test, and this section runs the two \
cheapest ones. (The stricter pathwise and detector-statistics tests live in \
the appendix.)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],

Cell["\<\
The first test isolates the deterministic error. Set the efficiency to zero: \
the channel still dephases the qubit, but no information enters, so every \
record is identical and the trajectory reduces to the master equation with no \
random scatter. Define the trace distance between two states, halve the step \
repeatedly, and watch the distance from the master-equation answer:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"traceDistance", "[", 
     RowBox[{"firstState_", ",", " ", "secondState_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
    "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
      RowBox[{"SingularValueList", "[", 
       RowBox[{"N", "[", 
        RowBox[{"firstState", " ", "-", " ", "secondState"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
      "]"}], "/", "2"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"observedOrders", "[", "errors_Association", "]"}], " ", ":=", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Most", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Keys", "[", "errors", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Log", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Most", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Values", "[", "errors", "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"Rest", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Values", "[", "errors", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}],
    ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"deterministicSteps", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0.08", ",", " ", "0.04", ",", " ", "0.02", ",", " ", "0.01"}], 
    "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"deterministicErrors", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
     RowBox[{"deterministicSteps", ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"traceDistance", "[", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Last", "@", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
             RowBox[{
             "initialState", ",", " ", "hamiltonian", ",", " ", 
              "measuredOperators", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", "0.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", "\n", "         ", "#", ",", " ", 
              "finalTime"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n",
           "      ", 
          RowBox[{"masterSolution", "[", "finalTime", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
        "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "deterministicSteps"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<errors\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "deterministicErrors"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<orders\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"observedOrders", "[", "deterministicErrors", "]"}]}]}], 
  "|>"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[36]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, the error falls in a regular way and the estimated order sits \
near one: halving the step roughly halves the error, the mark of a \
first-order scheme. This test matters most when the Hamiltonian is fast, but \
it says nothing about the random part.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The second test is the one we already passed in Part III, stated as a \
criterion: the mean over many records must approach the master equation, and \
the gap must be consistent with Monte Carlo scatter rather than a fixed bias. \
We saw the gap shrink toward the solver curve; increasing the number of \
records shrinks it further. Positivity, deterministic convergence, and the \
correct ensemble mean answer three different questions, and a step you trust \
has to pass all three. There is no universal good value of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],
 ": a step is adequate only relative to a stated model, time interval, \
detector bandwidth, and accuracy goal."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],

Cell["Appendix: Certifying a Step Size", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],

Cell["\<\
The two checks in Part VIII are enough for the physics above. Certifying a \
step size for research needs two stricter tools, gathered here so the main \
story stays uncluttered.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],

Cell["\<\
The first is pathwise convergence. Two independently sampled trajectories \
represent different detector histories and must not be compared point by \
point; to refine honestly, sample the finest Wiener increments once and build \
every coarser record by summing adjacent fine increments. This shares a \
single underlying noise path across resolutions:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"coarsenIncrements", "[", 
     RowBox[{"increments_", ",", " ", "blockSize_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Total", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Partition", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"N", "[", "increments", "]"}], ",", " ", "blockSize"}], 
      "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"coupledFamily", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "initialState_", ",", " ", "hamiltonian_", ",", " ", "monitored_", ",", 
      " ", "efficiencies_", ",", " ", "finestStep_", ",", "\n", "   ", 
      "finalTime_", ",", " ", "blockSizes_", ",", " ", "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", 
    ":=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"stepCount", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
          RowBox[{"finalTime", "/", "finestStep"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        "fineSteps", ",", " ", "fineNoise"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"fineSteps", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
         RowBox[{"finestStep", ",", " ", "stepCount"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
       "  ", 
       RowBox[{"fineNoise", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
             RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "finestStep", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
            "     ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"stepCount", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Length", "[", "monitored", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
         "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
       RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"N", "[", 
          RowBox[{"finestStep", " ", "blockSizes"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
         
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
           RowBox[{"block", ",", "\n", "     ", 
            RowBox[{"With", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"steps", " ", "=", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"coarsenIncrements", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"fineSteps", ",", " ", "block"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
                "\n", "       ", 
                RowBox[{"noise", " ", "=", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"coarsenIncrements", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"fineNoise", ",", " ", "block"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], 
              ",", "\n", "      ", 
              RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"step", " ", "=", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"rouchonStep", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "hamiltonian", ",", " ", "monitored", ",", " ", 
                    "efficiencies", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"steps", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
                  "        ", "states"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"states", " ", "=", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", "\n", "         ", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"state", ",", " ", "dW"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
                    "          ", 
                    RowBox[{"step", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"state", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"readoutIncrement", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "state", ",", " ", "monitored", ",", " ", "efficiencies", 
                    ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"steps", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "dW"}], "]"}]}],
                     "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "         ", "initialState", ",",
                     " ", "noise"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "       ", 
                 RowBox[{"<|", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"\"\<States\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "states"}], ",", 
                   " ", 
                   RowBox[{"\"\<Noise\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "noise"}]}], 
                  "|>"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
          "blockSizes"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"adjacentErrors", "[", "family_Association", "]"}], " ", ":=", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"stepValues", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Keys", "[", "family", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"trajectories", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Values", "[", "family", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "ratios"}], 
       "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ratios", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Most", "[", "stepValues", "]"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"Rest", "[", "stepValues", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
       "  ", 
       RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Most", "[", "stepValues", "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
         RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"pair", ",", " ", "ratio"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
             
             RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
              RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
               RowBox[{"traceDistance", ",", "\n", "       ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"pair", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<States\>\"", 
                   "]"}], ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"pair", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<States\>\"", 
                    "]"}], "[", 
                   RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "ratio"}], "]"}], 
                   "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Partition", "[", 
              RowBox[{"trajectories", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",",
              " ", "ratios"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rootMeanSquare", "[", "errorList_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"keys", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Keys", "@", 
        RowBox[{"First", "[", "errorList", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
      RowBox[{"keys", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"Values", " ", "/@", " ", "errorList"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}],
          "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[37]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],

Cell["\<\
Run four resolutions across sixty-four independent noise paths, sharing noise \
within each family, and estimate the order from the root-mean-square error \
over paths:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"families", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"coupledFamily", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "initialState", ",", " ", "hamiltonian", ",", " ", "measuredOperators", 
       ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "1.0", "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", "0.0025", ",", " ", 
       "2.0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"8", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"101", ",", " ", "164"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"maximumErrors", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rootMeanSquare", "[", 
     RowBox[{"adjacentErrors", " ", "/@", " ", "families"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<errors\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "maximumErrors"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<orders\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"observedOrders", "[", "maximumErrors", "]"}]}]}], 
  "|>"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[38]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],

Cell["\<\
The error decreases through the refinements and the order is close to one, so \
for this single monitored channel the scheme is first order pathwise, not \
merely positive.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The second tool checks the detector record against the state that generated \
it. For a simulated record, subtract the predicted signal and divide by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],
 "; this residual of the record against its own prediction (its innovation, \
in the language of filtering) should reproduce the standard-normal samples \
the simulator drew,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["r", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "-", 
      SqrtBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], 
      StyleBox["Tr",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "+", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],

Cell["\<\
Form these residuals for a simulated record and read their mean, variance, \
and lag-one correlation:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"normalizedInnovations", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "run_Association", ",", " ", "monitored_", ",", " ", "efficiencies_"}], 
     "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"state", ",", " ", "record", ",", " ", "dt"}], "}"}], ",", 
        "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"record", " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"readoutIncrement", "[", 
            RowBox[{
            "state", ",", " ", "monitored", ",", " ", "efficiencies", ",", 
             " ", "dt", ",", "\n", "        ", 
             RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
              RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Length", "[", "monitored", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
          ")"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "dt", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Most", "[", 
         RowBox[{"run", "[", "\"\<States\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"run", "[", "\"\<Record\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Differences", "[", 
         RowBox[{"run", "[", "\"\<Times\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
     "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"innovationRun", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "55", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"simulate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "initialState", ",", " ", "hamiltonian", ",", " ", "measuredOperators", 
       ",", " ", "0.0025", ",", " ", "5.0"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"innovations", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
     RowBox[{"normalizedInnovations", "[", 
      RowBox[{"innovationRun", ",", " ", "measuredOperators", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "1.0", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<mean\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "innovations", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<variance\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Variance", "[", "innovations", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<lag-one correlation\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Correlation", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Most", "[", "innovations", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Rest", "[", "innovations", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "|>"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[39]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],

Cell["\<\
The residuals have mean near zero, variance near one, and negligible lag-one \
correlation: the record generator draws fresh, independent noise, exactly as \
the model demands. This check validates the record and its pairing with the \
pre-step state; it does not replace the pathwise test.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A last caution, because it is a real trap. The compact Rouchon step was \
built from a first-order argument stated for commuting monitored operators, \
and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],
 " do not commute. The step stays positive by construction here, as Part II \
guaranteed for any channels, but that positivity does not certify the \
convergence order. Monitor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],
 " at once and measure the order instead of assuming it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ncMeasured", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "0.2", "]"}], " ", "X"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "0.3", "]"}], " ", "Z"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ncFamilies", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"coupledFamily", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "ketPlus", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"0.3", " ", "Y"}], ",", " ", "ncMeasured", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.8", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", "0.0025",
        ",", " ", "1.0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"8", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"301", ",", " ", "332"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ncErrors", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rootMeanSquare", "[", 
     RowBox[{"adjacentErrors", " ", "/@", " ", "ncFamilies"}], "]"}]}], ";"}],
   "\n"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<errors\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "ncErrors"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<orders\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"observedOrders", "[", "ncErrors", "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[40]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],

Cell["\<\
The trace distances still fall, but the measured order is visibly below one. \
The lesson is not to copy a convergence order from one model to another: when \
the monitored operators fail to commute, the step still gives a physical \
state, but you must measure its accuracy for yourself.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We built, from plain matrices, a positivity-preserving step for the \
conditional master equation, a ",
 Cell[BoxData["simulate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],
 " that manufactures synthetic records and their state paths and an ",
 Cell[BoxData["infer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],
 " that reconstructs a state path from a record it did not generate, an \
independent master-equation solver to check against, and a small kit for \
reading a detector current. With those, we watched a single record jitter \
while its average rebuilt the smooth master equation, saw strong monitoring \
freeze a qubit and weak monitoring free it, sent monitored emission wandering \
over the Bloch sphere, pulled a spectral peak out of a noisy current, dialed \
efficiency down to mix the conditional state, and ran the whole story \
unchanged in three dimensions."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The natural next steps live alongside this notebook. To do something with \
the record rather than only observe it, the sibling notebook on record \
analysis and feedback estimates the state in real time and feeds it back. To \
leave the discrete Hilbert space for a particle on a line, the \
continuous-space notebooks replace the qubit with a monitored position. And \
to close the loop with a real experiment, replace the synthetic readout here \
with calibrated detector increments in ",
 Cell[BoxData["infer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],
 ", and reserve part of the data for an independent test: continuous records \
have been used to estimate mechanical quantum states in real time and checked \
against later or separate measurements (",
 ButtonBox["Magrini et al., Nature 595, 373 (2021)",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-021-03602-3"], None}],
 "; ",
 ButtonBox["Rossi et al., Phys. Rev. Lett. 123, 163601 (2019)",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.123.\
163601"], None}],
 "). A synthetic trajectory in this notebook does not inherit that status; it \
earns only the right to be checked, which is what we did throughout."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],

Cell["Acknowledgment", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The state update follows the positivity-preserving scheme of Rouchon and \
Ralph. The examples use standard models of monitored ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],
 " noise and homodyne-detected emission. If you have suggestions or \
questions, reach out at ",
 ButtonBox["quantum@wolfram.com",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["mailto:quantum@wolfram.com"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"]
},
